1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Veridict. AI writes the code. Math approves the merge.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Three steps. One signature. Spec → synth → verify → credential → ZK proof → merge.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
A maintainer types a spec.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Claude generates the implementation, pytest suite, and Z3 invariants.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:34,000
On GitHub, the PR opens automatically. zk-review-gate is pending. Merge is blocked.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The reviewer opens it in Veridict. mypy, pytest, Z3 — all three formal layers green.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Tick reviewed. Click approve anonymously.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The Longfellow prover runs — about 14 seconds. The proof is bound to this exact commit SHA.

9
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Receipt. Proof accepted. 1 of 1 valid. Merge gate green. Identity never transmitted.

10
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Back on GitHub. Anonymous bot comment with ZK-verified attestations. Status check now green.

11
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Merge pull request. Confirm.

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Merged. AI synthesis, formally verified, anonymously approved.
